      "summaries": {
        "en": "Financial-services is a collection of open-source tools and templates from Anthropic for building AI-powered financial applications. It leverages Claude's capabilities for tasks like document analysis, risk assessment, and customer support. The project provides reusable code patterns and best practices for integrating large language models into regulated workflows. Developers can use these resources to prototype compliance-aware chatbots, automate report generation, or enhance fraud detection systems with explainable AI.",
        "zh": "Anthropic推出的开源工具集Financial-services，旨在利用Claude模型构建金融AI应用。它通过可复用代码模板和最佳实践，降低大语言模型集成到受监管工作流的门槛，解决合规性、可解释性和数据安全等要求。核心优势包括内置文档分析、风险评估和客户支持示例，强调输出可控性与审计追踪。开发者可快速原型化合规智能客服、自动化报告生成或可解释欺诈检测系统，提升业务效率。",
        "es": "Financial-services is a collection of open-source tools and templates from Anthropic for building AI-powered financial applications. It leverages Claude's capabilities for tasks like document analysis, risk assessment, and customer support. The project provides reusable code patterns and best practices for integrating large language models into regulated workflows. Developers can use these resources to prototype compliance-aware chatbots, automate report generation, or enhance fraud detection systems with explainable AI.",
        "sections": {
          "why": "financial-services gives teams a dependable path to production-ready AI tooling.",
          "what": "Financial-services is a collection of open-source tools and templates from Anthropic for building AI-powered financial applications. It leverages Claude's capabilities for tasks like document analysis, risk assessment, and customer support. The project provides reusable code patterns and best practices for integrating large language models into regulated workflows. Developers can use these resources to prototype compliance-aware chatbots, automate report generation, or enhance fraud detection systems with explainable AI.",
          "how": "Review https://github.com/anthropics/financial-services for docs, run starter examples, and integrate with your pipeline or evaluation stack."
        }
